            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F002:F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposed edit correctly reflects the statutory qualification in subparagraph (B). While subparagraph (A) requires consumer reporting agencies described in both section 1681a(p) and (w) to make free annual disclosures upon request, subparagraph (B) limits the application of subparagraph (A) for section 1681a(p) agencies specifically to requests made using the centralized source established under section 211(c) of the Fair and Accurate Credit Transactions Act of 2003.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F002:F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposed summary incorrectly extends the centralized source requirement to nationwide specialty consumer reporting agencies described in section 1681a(w). Subparagraph (B) explicitly restricts that condition to consumer reporting agencies described in section 1681a(p), whereas section 1681a(w) agencies are subject to separate streamlined process regulations under subparagraph (C).\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
